SUMMARY:Sandy Hook Birding
DESCRIPTION:Autumn birding at the hook: we may encounter anything from shorebirds and terns to flycatchers\, sparrows\, and warblers. A wide variety of habitats ensure good bird diversity at one of the state’s best spots. Bring lunch and be prepared for walking over flat and sandy terrain. Led by Linda Mack\, Chris Daly\, and Jonathan Klizas. \nLocation: Meet at Parking Lot B\, about halfway down the lot by the bathrooms \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/sandy-hook-birding-32/
LOCATION:Sandy Hook – Lot B\, Hartshorne Drive\, Sandy Hook\, NJ\, 07732\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Sandy-Hook-Birding-09.2026-scaled.webp
GEO:40.4071808233;-73.9782969352
