SUMMARY:Hawk ID Mini-Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Struggling to separate a Sharp-shinned Hawk from a Cooper’s? Amazed when a Bald Eagle is spotted high in the sky where you see nothing? Learn how seasoned Hawk watchers spot and identify these magnificent birds. Join CMBO interpretive naturalists at the raptor capital of North America\, Cape May Point State Park. Meets at the East Shelter\, the picnic pavilion NEXT to the Hawkwatch Platform. NO preregistration required. Family-friendly \nCOST: FREE \nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \n  \n \n 
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/hawk-id-mini-workshop-9/2026-09-26/
LOCATION:Cape May Point State Park – East Shelter\, NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:Birding,Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/Hawk-ID-mini-Workshop_Eventbright_2160x1080.jpg
GEO:38.933008140108;-74.95813540732
END:VEVENT
