SUMMARY:Fall Migration Cruise
DESCRIPTION:Join CMBO naturalists to cruise through nearly inaccessible back-bay marshes from Cape May to Stone Harbor. This trip will be by boat (beginning and ending at Cape May) through protected back-bay waters where we will enjoy a great variety of waterbirds and raptors. The Osprey is a 37′ pontoon boat that has a comfortable enclosed cabin with large viewing windows\, a front deck with a railing\, and a restroom on board. Non-motorized wheelchair accessible. More information\, detailed directions\, and online reservations at www.ospreycruise.com or call the Osprey at 609-898-3500. All trips depart from the Miss Chris Marina in Cape May. Free parking. Family-friendly. Preregistration is suggested. \nCost: $43 members\, $48 nonmembers\, child (12 & under) $28 \nREGISTER HERE \n 
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/fall-migration-cruise-5/2026-09-26/
LOCATION:Miss Chris Marina – The Osprey\, 1212 Wilson Dr\, Cape May\, NJ 08204\, NJ\, United States
CATEGORIES:Birding,Boat Trip,Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Family Program
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/Fall-Migration-Cruise_Eventbright_2160x1080.jpg
GEO:38.9501954;-74.910504
