SUMMARY:🦋 Monarch Fest at SHEF 🦋
DESCRIPTION:Scherman Hoffman is excited to join the Somerset Hills Education Foundation’s 30th Anniversary Celebration on Saturday\, September 26th\, 3:00 – 7:00 PM at the polo fields outside BES/BMS on Seney Drive! This family-friendly\, festival-style event brings together our five district towns — Bernardsville\, Far Hills\, Peapack\, Gladstone\, and Bedminster — to celebrate 30 years of educational innovation.\n \nStop by our NJA table for a mini version of our Monarch Festival! 🧡🦋 We’ll have: \n\nMonarchs raised in captivity\nLive tagging demonstrations\nMonarch education materials\nCrafts and butterfly glitter tattoos (by donation to NJA)\n\nOur Scherman Hoffman staff will be on hand to share all about our Sanctuary\, which borders the event grounds — come say hello and learn more about your wild neighbors! \nCOST: $10 adult / $8 senior / $35 family \nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \nLOCATION: Polo Fields\, outside BES/BMS \nFor more information Somerset Hills Education Foundation (SHEF) Events \nREGISTER HERE \n 
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/%f0%9f%a6%8b-monarch-fest-at-shef-%f0%9f%a6%8b/
LOCATION:Polo Grounds/Rec.Area/Municipal Park – Bernardsville\, 169 Seney Dr Ext\, Bernardsville\, NJ\, 07924\, United States
CATEGORIES:Event,Family Program,Monarchs,Scherman Hoffman Wildlife Sanctuary
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Monarch-Madness-10.2025.jpg
GEO:40.7325831032;-74.5676307193
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=DESCRIPTION:Scherman Hoffman is excited to join the Somerset Hills Education Foundation’s 30th Anniversary Celebration on Saturday September 26th 3:00 – 7:00 PM at the polo fields outside BES/BMS on Seney Drive! This family-friendly festival-style event brings together our five district towns — Bernardsville Far Hills Peapack Gladstone and Bedminster — to celebrate 30 years of educational innovation.\n \nStop by our NJA table for a mini version of our Monarch Festival! 🧡🦋 We’ll have: \n\nMonarchs raised in captivity\nLive tagging demonstrations\nMonarch education materials\nCrafts and butterfly glitter tattoos (by donation to NJA)\n\nOur Scherman Hoffman staff will be on hand to share all about our Sanctuary which borders the event grounds — come say hello and learn more about your wild neighbors! \nCOST: $10 adult / $8 senior / $35 family \nInterested in becoming a member? Please click on the following link to learn more or join: Become a Member today! \n Polo Fields outside BES/BMS \nFor more information Somerset Hills Education Foundation (SHEF) Events \nREGISTER HERE \n ;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=169 Seney Dr Ext:geo:-74.5676307193,40.7325831032
