SUMMARY:Monarch Festival 2026
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy music\, food\, and monarch tagging demonstrations. Make a craft to take home along with a monarch-themed souvenir from a local vendor. Discover what you can do to help protect these beautiful butterflies! Enjoy the following special programming and more at this year’s festival! \n\nButterfly Yoga with Itswell Yoga at 10am\nButterfly Parade at 3pm (everyone is invited to participate!)\nAll Day: Educational programs\, family-friendly games and activities\, local artists and authors\, Monarch Monitoring Project tagging demos\n\nWHERE: 1600 Delaware Avenue\, Cape May\, NJ 08204 \nWHEN: \n\nSunday\, September 27th\, 2026\n10:00 AM to 4:00 PM\n\nCOST: \n\nSuggested $5 donation per person. Cash donations accepted at event entry. Credit cards accepted inside visitor center.\n\nPlease note you do NOT need to present ticket at entry. Your registration through Eventbrite simply ensures you will receive important event updates if necessary. \n\n\nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/monarch-festival-2026/
LOCATION:Nature Center of Cape May\, 1600 Delaware Avenue\, Cape May\, NJ\, 08204\, United States
CATEGORIES:Cape May Bird Observatory,Cape May Bird Observatory's Northwood Center,Monarchs,Nature Center of Cape May
