SUMMARY:Forsythe (Brigantine) NWR
DESCRIPTION:Early fall birding at one of the state’s best hotspots. Expect a wide range of species from long-legged wading birds to raptors\, rails\, and many species of shorebirds\, terns\, and passerines. Each week is likely to be different as we watch the ebb and flow of fall migration. Wear long pants and a lightweight long-sleeved shirt. Insect repellant is advised. Restrooms on site. Bring lunch. Led by Mike Mandracchia and Hank Burk. \nLocation: 800 Great Creek Road\, Oceanville\, Forsythe NWR at main lot by headquarters. \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/forsythe-brigantine-nwr-78/
LOCATION:Edwin B Forsythe National Wildlife Refuge Admin Building And Visitor Contact Station\, 800 Great Creek Road\, Galloway\, NJ\, 08205\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://njaudubon.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Forsythe-Brigantine-NWR-09.2026.jpg
GEO:39.4646785;-74.449792
